Summary of Part One
The work in Part One1 can be summarized in the following four aspects:
1. Capable of handling non-uniform spacing and high signal-to-noise ratio data; 2. Adaptable to data with relatively large sampling time steps; 3. Explicitly derives interpretable and concise models with fewer parameters; 4. Highly flexible network structure that can readily incorporate new methods.
